            "name": "count",
            "type": "boolean",
            "required": false,
            "binding": "/query/count",
            "description": "Defaults to `true`. Set to `false` to skip the `COUNT(*)` behind `total_count`; the field is then omitted from the response."
          },
          {
            "name": "fields",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "binding": "/query/fields",
            "description": "Comma-separated list of fields to return on each row. Fields you don't request are left out of the response instead of coming back as `null`, so a missing key means you didn't ask for it and `null` means the value is null. `id` is always included, whether or not you name it. Pass `all` to get every requestable field. An unknown field name returns `400` with the list of valid names and the closest match, so a typo is caught instead of being silently ignored. Requestable here: `created_at`, `default_value`, `description`, `display_name`, `external_id`, `external_source`, `id`, `is_active`, `is_multi`, `is_required`, `logo_props`, `name`, `options`, `property_type`, `relation_type`, `settings`, `updated_at`, `updated_by_id`, `validation_rules`. See [Sparse fields](/api-reference/v2/sparse-fields)."
